<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Nairi</h1><p class="st-meta">1200 BCE – 850 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nairi, a loose confederation of highland chiefdoms around Lake Van that fought Assyria and became the seedbed of Urartu.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Nairi was the Assyrian name for the mountain lands north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age-collapse">Late Bronze Age collapse</a>, local chiefdoms of the region formed temporary coalitions to resist Assyrian raids, first recorded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-i">Tiglath-Pileser I</a> c. 1100 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-i">Tiglath-Pileser I</a> claimed to have defeated 23 kings of Nairi and set up an inscription near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malazgirt">Malazgirt</a>. Nairi had no capital; it was a patchwork of fortified villages living from herding, farming and metalworking, which paid tribute in horses and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Repeated Assyrian campaigns under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurnasirpal-ii">Ashurnasirpal II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> pushed the Nairi chiefdoms to unite. By the mid-9th century BCE most were absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Kingdom of Urartu</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1200 BCE – 850 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:35.82%;width:6.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1200 BCE – 850 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hurro-Urartian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey, Armenia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nairi lands</dd></dl></aside></div>
